-
-First, set up a base Python environment on
-your system. We highly recommend using miniconda or
-mambaforge to easily install all the dependencies.
-
-To install the stable version of the package:
-
-.. code-block:: bash
-
-    pip install miles-guess
-
-To use the latest developed version of the package,
-first download :
-
-.. code-block:: bash
+This source distribution targets Python 3.11 and NumPy 2. The audited CPU
+runtime uses Python 3.11.17, PyTorch 2.14.1, and NumPy 2.4.6. Native PyTorch
+requires no Keras or TensorFlow installation. Install this local source
+package to obtain the modernization; the public PyPI package is separate.
 
-    git clone git@github.com:ai2es/miles-guess.git
-    cd miles-guess
-
