+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "classifier-00",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "# Evidential classification: train, validate, then test\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This CPU tutorial trains the package's `CategoricalDNN` and original EDL digamma\n",
+    "loss on three overlapping synthetic classes. It requires no downloads and runs in\n",
+    "about a minute on a typical CPU. It demonstrates the workflow, not the paper's\n",
+    "precipitation-type benchmark.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Install in a Python 3.11 environment with `python -m pip install -e \".[torch,notebooks]\"`,\n",
+    "select that environment's Jupyter kernel, then **Restart Kernel and Run All**.\n",
+    "The installed package is imported without working-directory assumptions.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The 60% training partition fits preprocessing and model weights; 20% validation\n",
+    "selects the best predictive log loss; the final 20% is an untouched test set.\n",
+    "All settings are fixed before that test set is evaluated.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Based on the original MILES-GUESS examples by John Schreck, David John Gagne, Charlie Becker, Gabrielle Gantos, Dhamma Kimpara, and Thomas Martin. This modernized tutorial uses new synthetic data and preserves the package's scientific loss.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 1,
+   "id": "classifier-01",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "Python 3.11.17 | PyTorch 2.14.1+cpu | NumPy 2.4.6 | SciPy 1.17.1 | device: cpu\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "import copy\n",
+    "import platform\n",
+    "import time\n",
+    "\n",
+    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
+    "import numpy as np\n",
+    "import pandas as pd\n",
+    "import scipy\n",
+    "import torch\n",
+    "from IPython.display import display\n",
+    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
+    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
+    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset\n",
+    "\n",
+    "SEED = 2026\n",
+    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
+    "torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
+    "torch.set_num_threads(2)\n",
+    "device = torch.device(\"cpu\")\n",
+    "plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.dpi\": 110, \"font.size\": 10, \"axes.spines.top\": False,\n",
+    "                     \"axes.spines.right\": False, \"axes.grid\": True, \"grid.alpha\": 0.2})\n",
+    "print(f\"Python {platform.python_version()} | PyTorch {torch.__version__} | \"\n",
+    "      f\"NumPy {np.__version__} | SciPy {scipy.__version__} | device: {device}\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "from sklearn.datasets import make_blobs\n",
+    "from mlguess.torch.models import CategoricalDNN\n",
+    "from mlguess.torch.class_losses import edl_digamma_loss\n",
+    "from mlguess.evaluation import evaluate_classifier\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "classifier-02",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 1. Make three overlapping classes and split before scaling\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The classes overlap deliberately: some uncertainty is irreducible from these two\n",
+    "features. Stratification retains class representation in each partition. Independent\n",
+    "rows justify a random split here; grouped subjects, stations, and time series need a\n",
+    "group or chronological split instead. All input scaling is fitted on training rows.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 2,
+   "id": "classifier-03",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "Rows: train=1440, validation=480, reserved test=480\n"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "image/png": "",
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<Figure size 770x440 with 1 Axes>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "display_data"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "X, y = make_blobs(n_samples=2400, centers=[[-1.7, -0.7], [1.5, -0.7], [0.0, 1.6]],\n",
+    "                  cluster_std=[0.85, 0.95, 0.90], random_state=SEED)\n",
+    "num_classes = 3\n",
+    "class_names = np.array([\"Class 0\", \"Class 1\", \"Class 2\"])\n",
+    "colors = [\"#0072B2\", \"#D55E00\", \"#009E73\"]\n",
+    "development, test_idx = train_test_split(np.arange(len(X)), test_size=0.20,\n",
+    "                                        stratify=y, random_state=SEED)\n",
+    "train_idx, valid_idx = train_test_split(development, test_size=0.25,\n",
+    "                                       stratify=y[development], random_state=SEED + 1)\n",
+    "assert not (set(train_idx) & set(valid_idx) or set(train_idx) & set(test_idx)\n",
+    "            or set(valid_idx) & set(test_idx))\n",
+    "print(f\"Rows: train={len(train_idx)}, validation={len(valid_idx)}, reserved test={len(test_idx)}\")\n",
+    "x_scaler = StandardScaler().fit(X[train_idx])\n",
+    "as_tensor = lambda array: torch.as_tensor(array, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n",
+    "x_train = as_tensor(x_scaler.transform(X[train_idx]))\n",
+    "x_valid = as_tensor(x_scaler.transform(X[valid_idx]))\n",
+    "y_train = torch.as_tensor(y[train_idx], dtype=torch.long, device=device)\n",
+    "y_valid = torch.as_tensor(y[valid_idx], dtype=torch.long, device=device)\n",
+    "loader = DataLoader(TensorDataset(x_train, y_train), batch_size=128, shuffle=True,\n",
+    "                    generator=torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED), num_workers=0)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
+    "for k in range(num_classes):\n",
+    "    rows = train_idx[y[train_idx] == k]\n",
+    "    ax.scatter(X[rows, 0], X[rows, 1], s=12, alpha=0.4, color=colors[k], label=class_names[k])\n",
+    "ax.set(title=\"Training observations only\", xlabel=\"Feature 1\", ylabel=\"Feature 2\")\n",
+    "ax.legend(); plt.show()\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "classifier-04",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 2. Train evidence and select by validation log loss\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Raw network outputs become nonnegative evidence through ReLU. The Dirichlet\n",
+    "concentrations are $\\alpha_k=\\operatorname{ReLU}(z_k)+1$, and predictive class\n",
+    "probabilities are $p_k=\\alpha_k/\\sum_j\\alpha_j$. Do not apply softmax to the\n",
+    "evidence head. The EDL loss receives one-hot targets and the explicit `device`\n",
+    "keyword; its KL regularizer is annealed over the first 25 epochs.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The validation score is predictive log loss without the annealed penalty. This\n",
+    "makes checkpoint scores comparable across epochs. We retain the package's loss\n",
+    "formula and do not tune on the test set.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 3,
+   "id": "classifier-05",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "Frozen validation-selected epoch 197; trained 200 epochs in 4.7 s. No test predictions made yet.\n"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "image/png": "",
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<Figure size 1210x374 with 2 Axes>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "display_data"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
+    "model = CategoricalDNN(input_size=2, output_size=num_classes, layer_size=[64, 64],\n",
+    "                       dr=[0.0, 0.0], batch_norm=False, softmax=False).to(device)\n",
+    "optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.003)\n",
+    "max_epochs, patience, annealing_step = 200, 40, 25\n",
+    "history, best_score, best_epoch, best_state = [], float(\"inf\"), 0, None\n",
+    "started = time.perf_counter()\n",
+    "\n",
+    "for epoch in range(1, max_epochs + 1):\n",
+    "    model.train()\n",
+    "    loss_sum = 0.0\n",
+    "    for xb, yb in loader:\n",
+    "        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
+    "        target = torch.nn.functional.one_hot(yb, num_classes=num_classes).float()\n",
+    "        loss = edl_digamma_loss(model(xb), target, epoch_num=epoch,\n",
+    "                                num_classes=num_classes, annealing_step=annealing_step,\n",
+    "                                device=device)\n",
+    "        if not torch.isfinite(loss):\n",
+    "            raise RuntimeError(\"Non-finite training loss\")\n",
+    "        loss.backward()\n",
+    "        optimizer.step()\n",
+    "        loss_sum += loss.item() * len(xb)\n",
+    "    model.eval()\n",
+    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
+    "        alpha = torch.relu(model(x_valid)) + 1.0\n",
+    "        p_valid = alpha / alpha.sum(dim=1, keepdim=True)\n",
+    "        valid_log_loss = -p_valid[torch.arange(len(y_valid)), y_valid].log().mean().item()\n",
+    "    history.append({\"epoch\": epoch, \"train_objective\": loss_sum / len(x_train),\n",
+    "                    \"valid_log_loss\": valid_log_loss})\n",
+    "    if valid_log_loss < best_score:\n",
+    "        best_score, best_epoch, best_state = valid_log_loss, epoch, copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())\n",
+    "    if epoch - best_epoch >= patience:\n",
+    "        break\n",
+    "\n",
+    "assert best_state is not None\n",
+    "model.load_state_dict(best_state)\n",
+    "model.eval()\n",
+    "model.requires_grad_(False)\n",
+    "history = pd.DataFrame(history)\n",
+    "print(f\"Frozen validation-selected epoch {best_epoch}; trained {len(history)} epochs \"\n",
+    "      f\"in {time.perf_counter() - started:.1f} s. No test predictions made yet.\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 3.4))\n",
+    "axes[0].plot(history.epoch, history.train_objective, color=\"#0072B2\")\n",
+    "axes[0].set(title=\"EDL training objective (annealed KL)\", xlabel=\"Epoch\", ylabel=\"Objective\")\n",
+    "axes[1].plot(history.epoch, history.valid_log_loss, color=\"#D55E00\")\n",
+    "axes[1].axvline(best_epoch, color=\"black\", linestyle=\"--\", label=f\"Selected: {best_epoch}\")\n",
+    "axes[1].set(title=\"Validation predictive log loss\", xlabel=\"Epoch\", ylabel=\"Log loss\")\n",
+    "axes[1].legend(); fig.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "classifier-06",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 3. Freeze, then evaluate the untouched test partition\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Accuracy measures hard-label correctness. Log loss and the multiclass Brier score\n",
+    "measure probabilistic predictions; smaller is better. Here Brier is the **sum** of\n",
+    "squared probability errors over classes, averaged over observations. ECE is a\n",
+    "10-bin, count-weighted top-label calibration error. Its value depends on binning\n",
+    "and sample size, so inspect the reliability diagram and bin counts as well.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For each class indicator, with $S=\\sum_k\\alpha_k$,\n",
+    "$A_k=p_k(1-p_k)S/(S+1)$ and $E_k=p_k(1-p_k)/(S+1)$.\n",
+    "Their sum is $p_k(1-p_k)$ by the law of total variance. These are marginal\n",
+    "indicator variances; they are not a scalar variance of numeric class labels.\n",
+    "The separate quantity $u=K/S$ is an evidence-based uncertainty score, not a probability of error.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 4,
+   "id": "classifier-07",
