+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "regression-00",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "# Evidential regression: train, validate, then test\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This small CPU tutorial trains the package's `DNN` with its original\n",
+    "`EvidentialRegressionLoss` on a synthetic nonlinear problem with varying noise.\n",
+    "It requires no downloads and takes about a minute on a typical CPU. The goal is\n",
+    "to demonstrate a reproducible workflow, not to reproduce the paper's weather benchmark.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Install the package and notebook dependencies in your Python 3.11 environment:\n",
+    "`python -m pip install -e \".[torch,notebooks]\"`. Select that environment's Jupyter\n",
+    "kernel, then **Restart Kernel and Run All**. The notebook uses the installed package\n",
+    "and works from either the repository root or the notebook directory.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The 60% training set fits scalers and model weights. The 20% validation set chooses\n",
+    "the checkpoint. The remaining 20% test set is opened only after the model is frozen;\n",
+    "its results are diagnostics, never a signal for choosing a better run.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Based on the original MILES-GUESS examples by John Schreck, David John Gagne, Charlie Becker, Gabrielle Gantos, Dhamma Kimpara, and Thomas Martin. This modernized tutorial uses new synthetic data and preserves the package's scientific loss.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 1,
+   "id": "regression-01",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "Python 3.11.17 | PyTorch 2.14.1+cpu | NumPy 2.4.6 | SciPy 1.17.1 | device: cpu\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "import copy\n",
+    "import platform\n",
+    "import time\n",
+    "\n",
+    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
+    "import numpy as np\n",
+    "import pandas as pd\n",
+    "import scipy\n",
+    "import torch\n",
+    "from IPython.display import display\n",
+    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
+    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
+    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset\n",
+    "\n",
+    "SEED = 2026\n",
+    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
+    "torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
+    "torch.set_num_threads(2)\n",
+    "device = torch.device(\"cpu\")\n",
+    "plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.dpi\": 110, \"font.size\": 10, \"axes.spines.top\": False,\n",
+    "                     \"axes.spines.right\": False, \"axes.grid\": True, \"grid.alpha\": 0.2})\n",
+    "print(f\"Python {platform.python_version()} | PyTorch {torch.__version__} | \"\n",
+    "      f\"NumPy {np.__version__} | SciPy {scipy.__version__} | device: {device}\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "from mlguess.torch.models import DNN\n",
+    "from mlguess.torch.regression_losses import EvidentialRegressionLoss\n",
+    "from mlguess.evaluation import evaluate_nig\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "regression-02",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 1. Generate data and reserve independent rows\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Here each row is an independent observation, so a random split is appropriate.\n",
+    "For weather stations, repeated subjects, or time series, replace this with a group\n",
+    "or chronological split before fitting anything. The known generating mean and noise\n",
+    "are available only because this is a synthetic demonstration.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 2,
+   "id": "regression-03",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "Rows: train=1260, validation=420, reserved test=420\n"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "image/png": "",
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<Figure size 880x396 with 1 Axes>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "display_data"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "rng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n",
+    "X = rng.uniform(-3.0, 3.0, size=(2100, 1))\n",
+    "latent_mean = 0.5 * X[:, 0] + 0.7 * np.sin(1.3 * X[:, 0])\n",
+    "noise_sd = 0.15 + 0.20 / (1.0 + np.exp(-1.5 * X[:, 0]))\n",
+    "y = (latent_mean + rng.normal(size=len(X)) * noise_sd)[:, None]\n",
+    "\n",
+    "development, test_idx = train_test_split(np.arange(len(X)), test_size=0.20, random_state=SEED)\n",
+    "train_idx, valid_idx = train_test_split(development, test_size=0.25, random_state=SEED + 1)\n",
+    "assert not (set(train_idx) & set(valid_idx) or set(train_idx) & set(test_idx)\n",
+    "            or set(valid_idx) & set(test_idx))\n",
+    "print(f\"Rows: train={len(train_idx)}, validation={len(valid_idx)}, reserved test={len(test_idx)}\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "x_scaler = StandardScaler().fit(X[train_idx])\n",
+    "y_scaler = StandardScaler().fit(y[train_idx])\n",
+    "as_tensor = lambda array: torch.as_tensor(array, dtype=torch.float32, device=device)\n",
+    "x_train = as_tensor(x_scaler.transform(X[train_idx]))\n",
+    "y_train = as_tensor(y_scaler.transform(y[train_idx]))\n",
+    "x_valid = as_tensor(x_scaler.transform(X[valid_idx]))\n",
+    "y_valid = as_tensor(y_scaler.transform(y[valid_idx]))\n",
+    "loader = DataLoader(TensorDataset(x_train, y_train), batch_size=128, shuffle=True,\n",
+    "                    generator=torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED), num_workers=0)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 3.6))\n",
+    "ax.scatter(X[train_idx, 0], y[train_idx, 0], s=8, alpha=0.3, label=\"Training observations\")\n",
+    "order = np.argsort(X[train_idx, 0])\n",
+    "ax.plot(X[train_idx[order], 0], latent_mean[train_idx[order]], color=\"black\",\n",
+    "        linewidth=2, label=\"Generating mean\")\n",
+    "ax.set(xlabel=\"Input x\", ylabel=\"Target y\", title=\"Only training observations are shown\")\n",
+    "ax.legend(); plt.show()\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "regression-04",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 2. Fit the original NIG loss and select by validation NLL\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The head returns $(\\gamma,\\nu,\\alpha,\\beta)$. We retain the package's original\n",
+    "negative log likelihood plus evidence regularizer, with a fixed coefficient of 0.01.\n",
+    "Validation uses predictive negative log likelihood without that regularizer, so\n",
+    "checkpoint selection measures the predictive distribution. All settings are fixed\n",
+    "before looking at test results. Losses below are in standardized target units.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 3,
+   "id": "regression-05",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "Frozen validation-selected epoch 148; trained 188 epochs in 4.2 s. No test predictions made yet.\n"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "image/png": "",
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<Figure size 1210x374 with 2 Axes>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "display_data"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
+    "model = DNN(input_size=1, output_size=1, layer_size=[64, 64], dr=[0.0, 0.0],\n",
+    "            batch_norm=False, lng=True).to(device)\n",
+    "criterion = EvidentialRegressionLoss(coef=0.01)\n",
+    "optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.003)\n",
+    "max_epochs, patience = 220, 40\n",
+    "history, best_score, best_epoch, best_state = [], float(\"inf\"), 0, None\n",
+    "started = time.perf_counter()\n",
+    "\n",
+    "for epoch in range(1, max_epochs + 1):\n",
+    "    model.train()\n",
+    "    loss_sum = 0.0\n",
+    "    for xb, yb in loader:\n",
+    "        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
+    "        loss = criterion(*model(xb), yb)\n",
+    "        if not torch.isfinite(loss):\n",
+    "            raise RuntimeError(\"Non-finite training loss\")\n",
+    "        loss.backward()\n",
+    "        optimizer.step()\n",
+    "        loss_sum += loss.item() * len(xb)\n",
+    "    model.eval()\n",
+    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
+    "        gamma, nu, alpha, beta = model(x_valid)\n",
+    "        valid_nll = criterion.normal_inverse_gamma_nll(y_valid, gamma, nu, alpha, beta).mean().item()\n",
+    "    history.append({\"epoch\": epoch, \"train_objective\": loss_sum / len(x_train), \"valid_nll\": valid_nll})\n",
+    "    if valid_nll < best_score:\n",
+    "        best_score, best_epoch, best_state = valid_nll, epoch, copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())\n",
+    "    if epoch - best_epoch >= patience:\n",
+    "        break\n",
+    "\n",
+    "assert best_state is not None\n",
+    "model.load_state_dict(best_state)\n",
+    "model.eval()\n",
+    "model.requires_grad_(False)\n",
+    "history = pd.DataFrame(history)\n",
+    "print(f\"Frozen validation-selected epoch {best_epoch}; trained {len(history)} epochs \"\n",
+    "      f\"in {time.perf_counter() - started:.1f} s. No test predictions made yet.\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 3.4))\n",
+    "axes[0].plot(history.epoch, history.train_objective, color=\"#0072B2\")\n",
+    "axes[0].set(title=\"Training objective (NLL + regularizer)\", xlabel=\"Epoch\", ylabel=\"Objective\")\n",
+    "axes[1].plot(history.epoch, history.valid_nll, color=\"#D55E00\")\n",
+    "axes[1].axvline(best_epoch, color=\"black\", linestyle=\"--\", label=f\"Selected: {best_epoch}\")\n",
+    "axes[1].set(title=\"Validation predictive NLL\", xlabel=\"Epoch\", ylabel=\"NLL\")\n",
+    "axes[1].legend(); fig.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "regression-06",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 3. Open the test set once the model is frozen\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For one NIG prediction, the law of total variance gives\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$A=\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha-1},\\qquad\n",
+    "E=\\frac{\\beta}{\\nu(\\alpha-1)},\\qquad T=A+E.$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The predictive distribution is Student-t with degrees of freedom $2\\alpha$ and\n",
+    "scale $s=\\sqrt{\\beta(1+\\nu)/(\\nu\\alpha)}$. **This scale is not the predictive\n",
+    "standard deviation.** `evaluate_nig` converts the prediction back to target units,\n",
+    "then uses SciPy's Student-t `logpdf`, `cdf`, and `ppf` for NLL, PIT, and central\n",
+    "prediction intervals. These are intervals for a new observation, not confidence\n",
+    "intervals for the latent mean. Variances are multiplied by the square of the target scale.\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 4,
+   "id": "regression-07",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "All test metrics and intervals are in original target units.\n"
+     ]
+    },
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/html": [
+       "<div>\n",
+       "<style scoped>\n",
