+    "## 3. Freeze, then evaluate the untouched test partition\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Accuracy measures hard-label correctness. Log loss and the multiclass Brier score\n",
+    "measure probabilistic predictions; smaller is better. Here Brier is the **sum** of\n",
+    "squared probability errors over classes, averaged over observations. ECE is a\n",
+    "10-bin, count-weighted top-label calibration error. Its value depends on binning\n",
+    "and sample size, so inspect the reliability diagram and bin counts as well.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For each class indicator, with $S=\\sum_k\\alpha_k$,\n",
+    "$A_k=p_k(1-p_k)S/(S+1)$ and $E_k=p_k(1-p_k)/(S+1)$.\n",
+    "Their sum is $p_k(1-p_k)$ by the law of total variance. These are marginal\n",
+    "indicator variances; they are not a scalar variance of numeric class labels.\n",
+    "The separate quantity $u=K/S$ is an evidence-based uncertainty score, not a probability of error.\n"
    ]
   },
