+    "## 5. Does uncertainty identify difficult cases?\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Compare the evidence-based score between correct and incorrect predictions, then\n",
+    "sort test cases from lowest to highest uncertainty. The retention curve reports\n",
+    "error among the least-uncertain retained cases. This is a diagnostic ranking, not\n",
+    "a deployed rejection threshold: choosing a threshold requires validation data and\n",
+    "an application-specific cost. Higher uncertainty need not identify every error,\n",
+    "and no out-of-distribution guarantee is implied by this in-distribution example.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "In the stored run, many reliability points lie above the diagonal: the classifier is underconfident on this test set. The ECE and reliability counts report this directly. We leave the frozen predictions unchanged rather than using the test set to calibrate them.\n"
