+    "## Apply this to your data\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Replace `X` with a finite numeric matrix `(rows, features)` and `y` with integer\n",
+    "class indices `0, ..., K-1`; update class names and model sizes. Define any label\n",
+    "encoding from the intended class vocabulary or training data. Keep the test partition\n",
+    "out of preprocessing, checkpoint selection, calibration, and threshold tuning.\n",
+    "Report class counts and per-class results when classes are imbalanced.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The exact variance identity verifies the distributional calculation, not empirical\n",
+    "calibration or scientific identifiability of the two uncertainty components. For\n",
+    "dropout or model ensembles, use the package's documented hierarchical uncertainty\n",
+    "helpers: averaging only the member variance components omits between-member\n",
+    "disagreement. This tutorial uses one evidential model without dropout.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Scientific references: [Schreck et al., 2024](https://doi.org/10.1175/AIES-D-23-0093.1)\n",
