+    "\n",
+    "For one NIG prediction, the law of total variance gives\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$A=\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha-1},\\qquad\n",
+    "E=\\frac{\\beta}{\\nu(\\alpha-1)},\\qquad T=A+E.$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The predictive distribution is Student-t with degrees of freedom $2\\alpha$ and\n",
+    "scale $s=\\sqrt{\\beta(1+\\nu)/(\\nu\\alpha)}$. **This scale is not the predictive\n",
+    "standard deviation.** `evaluate_nig` converts the prediction back to target units,\n",
+    "then uses SciPy's Student-t `logpdf`, `cdf`, and `ppf` for NLL, PIT, and central\n",
+    "prediction intervals. These are intervals for a new observation, not confidence\n",
+    "intervals for the latent mean. Variances are multiplied by the square of the target scale.\n"
    ]
